{{also|Tänzen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|tanzen}}, from {{der|de|fro|dancer}}; the adapted onset ''t-'' in [[Upper German]] dialects (and standard German) proves that the word was not borrowed directly from the French word, but via {{der|de|gml|-}} or {{der|de|dum|dansen}} and [[Central German]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈtan(t)sən/|[-t͡sn̩]|[-sn̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-tanzen.ogg|audio (Austria)}}
* {{audio|de|De-tanzen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|<haben,sein>}}

# to [[dance]]

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj|<haben,sein>}}

====Usage notes====
* The perfect auxiliary is normally {{m|de||haben}}, but {{m|de||sein}} is used when there is a movement from place to place. For example: {{m|de||Wir sind durch die Straßen getanzt.|t=We danced through the streets}}.

